# Gole Number System Community Licence v1.0

How you may use the Gole Number System™, the Gole fonts, the Gole symbol artwork and the official Gole software. Free to use with attribution; conditions apply. The full terms are below.

**Effective:** November 27, 2026

Version 1.0, effective November 27, 2026. Copyright © 2026 eSetu Solutions Private Limited.

### Preamble

This Licence governs your use of the Gole Number System™ and the other Gole Materials made available by eSetu Solutions Private Limited, Hyderabad, India (“eSetu” or the “Licensor”).

By downloading, installing, accessing or using the Gole Materials, you agree to be bound by this Licence. Your acceptance in electronic form creates a binding contract under the Indian Contract Act, 1872 and the Information Technology Act, 2000. If you do not agree, do not use the Gole Materials.

Where this Licence and a signed agreement between you and eSetu differ, the signed agreement applies.

### 1. Definitions

*   **“Gole Materials”** means, together: (a) the Gole Number System, the base-100 notation in which each pair of decimal digits (00–99) is written as a single glyph built from a main symbol and a modifier symbol; (b) the Gole fonts, including `GoleStandard.ttf` and any WOFF or WOFF2 versions, their glyph outlines and OpenType ligature tables; (c) the Gole symbol artwork published by eSetu; (d) the Official Gole Software; and (e) the Gole documentation, including the Gole Knowledge Base, guides and published papers.
*   **“Official Gole Software”** means the Gole packages published by eSetu (for example on npm and PyPI), the Gole MCP server, and the converters and tools on esetu.in, excluding any package that eSetu releases under an open-source licence. The code of such a package is governed by its open-source licence alone. Using it to write, show or process numbers in the Gole Number System, or with the Gole fonts or symbol artwork, remains subject to this Licence, and its open-source licence grants no rights in the Gole Number System, the Gole fonts, the symbol artwork, the Gole Specification or any patent.
*   **“Gole Specification”** means the official glyph shapes, digit-pair mappings and rules of the Gole Number System as published by eSetu.
*   **“Entity”** means you or, if you act on behalf of a legal entity, that legal entity, together with its holding, subsidiary and associate companies within the meaning of the Companies Act, 2013 and every other person that controls it, is controlled by it or is under common control with it.
*   **“Financial Year”** means the period from 1 April to 31 March or, for an Entity outside India, its statutory accounting year.
*   **“Annual Turnover”** means the total consolidated gross revenue of the Entity from all sources, in and outside India and including export revenue, for its most recently completed Financial Year. It is taken from the Entity’s audited financial statements where an audit is required by law, and otherwise from its books of account. It excludes goods and services tax and other indirect taxes collected. Amounts in other currencies are converted into Indian rupees at the reference rate published for the last working day of that Financial Year by the Reserve Bank of India or Financial Benchmarks India Private Limited.
*   **“Threshold”** means ₹10,00,00,000 (Rupees ten crore).
*   **“Non-Commercial Use”** means any use that does not involve direct or indirect commercial benefit or revenue. It includes personal use, teaching in recognised schools, colleges and universities and in workshops run without profit, non-commercial academic or scientific research, and evaluation or prototyping.
*   **“Commercial Use”** means any use other than Non-Commercial Use. It includes: use in a product or service that is sold, licensed or offered to customers, such as software, SaaS, mobile apps, business websites and AI products; building Gole into hardware or devices, such as printers, displays, meters, clocks, IoT devices, POS terminals or vehicles; use in business operations, for example on receipts, labels, barcodes, tickets, logistics or financial documents; bundling or redistributing Gole Materials in a commercial offering; and using Gole Materials as training data for a commercial machine-learning model.

### 2. Grant of Rights

**2.1 Non-Commercial Use.** Subject to the terms of this Licence, eSetu grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free licence, for the full term of copyright in the Gole Materials, to use, reproduce and redistribute the Gole Materials, and to modify the Official Gole Software, for Non-Commercial Use.

**2.2 Commercial Use (Turnover-Capped).** Subject to the terms of this Licence, eSetu grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free licence to do the acts listed in clause 2.1 for Commercial Use, for as long as your Entity’s Annual Turnover is **less than the Threshold of ₹10 crore**.

**2.3 Commercial Use above the Threshold.** If your Entity’s Annual Turnover equals or exceeds the Threshold, Commercial Use of the Gole Materials is **not permitted** under this Licence. You must obtain a separate written commercial licence from eSetu before making any Commercial Use. Clause 4.3 applies to an Entity that crosses the Threshold while already using the Gole Materials.

**2.4 Work done for others.** If you use the Gole Materials on behalf of another Entity, or to build a product, device or service for it, clause 2.2 applies only if both your Entity and that other Entity are below the Threshold.

**2.5 Government and public sector.** A government department, statutory body or public sector undertaking, and anyone deploying the Gole Materials for one, needs a written licence from eSetu for Commercial Use, whatever its Annual Turnover.

**2.6 Patent licence.** eSetu grants you a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence under Indian Patent Application No. 202441034973, any patent granted on it and any corresponding application or patent in another country, only to the extent needed to exercise the rights granted in clauses 2.1 and 2.2. This patent licence ends automatically if your Entity starts or supports any patent claim against eSetu or any user of the Gole Materials that relates to the Gole Materials.

**2.7 Reservation.** All rights not expressly granted in this Licence are reserved by eSetu.

### 3. Conditions

*   **Attribution.** When you use or show the Gole Number System, credit it as: `Gole Number System™ by eSetu Solutions Pvt. Ltd. – https://esetu.in`. In academic work, also cite eSetu’s peer-reviewed paper on the Gole Number System published in the Indian Journal of Advanced Mathematics (IJAM). Any redistribution of Gole Materials must include this Licence and eSetu’s copyright notice.
*   **Integrity of the standard.** You may redistribute the Gole fonts and symbol artwork only in unmodified form. You must not publish altered glyph shapes, digit mappings or rules under the Gole name, or anything that could be confused with the official Gole Number System. Any modified version of the Official Gole Software that you distribute must still follow the Gole Specification, must be clearly marked as modified, and must not be presented as an eSetu release.
*   **No additional restrictions, no sublicensing.** You may not sublicense, sell or transfer your rights under this Licence. Each recipient of Gole Materials receives a licence directly from eSetu on these terms, and you may not impose any restriction on a recipient that contradicts them.
*   **Lawful and clear use.** You must use the Gole Materials in compliance with applicable law. Gole numerals do not replace numerals that the law requires. Where Indian law requires a quantity, price, date, amount or identifier to be shown in a prescribed form, for example under the Legal Metrology Act, 2009 and its rules, the goods and services tax invoicing rules or the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, you must show it in that form as well. You must not use Gole numerals to hide information from, or mislead, consumers, regulators or anyone else.
*   **No trademark licence.** This Licence gives you no right to the eSetu™ or Gole Number System™ names, the Gole emblem or the glyph marks beyond the attribution above. You must not suggest that eSetu endorses or partners with you without written permission. See the [Trademark Policy](https://www.esetu.in/trademark-policy).

### 4. Turnover Confirmation and Crossing the Threshold

**4.1 Self-assessment.** You are responsible for checking, after the end of each Financial Year, whether your Entity remains below the Threshold.

**4.2 Confirmation on request.** If you make Commercial Use of the Gole Materials, eSetu may ask you in writing, not more than once in a Financial Year, to confirm that your Entity is below the Threshold. Within 30 days you must provide either a certificate from a practising Chartered Accountant or the relevant extract of your Entity’s audited financial statements. eSetu will keep this information confidential and use it only to verify compliance with this Licence.

**4.3 Crossing the Threshold.** If your Entity’s Annual Turnover for a Financial Year equals or exceeds the Threshold, you have 180 days from the end of that Financial Year to obtain a written commercial licence from eSetu or stop all Commercial Use. Your use during that period remains licensed under clause 2.2.

**4.4 Falling back below the Threshold.** If your Entity’s Annual Turnover later falls below the Threshold, clause 2.2 applies to you again from the start of the next Financial Year, unless a signed agreement with eSetu says otherwise.

### 5. Termination

**5.1** This Licence ends automatically if you breach any of its terms and do not cure the breach within 30 days after eSetu notifies you of it. It ends immediately, without a cure period, on a second breach or on a breach of the “Integrity of the standard” condition in clause 3.

**5.2** When this Licence ends, you must stop all use of the Gole fonts, symbol artwork and Official Gole Software and delete all copies in your possession or control.

**5.3** Clauses 2.7, 5.2, 6 and 7 continue after this Licence ends.

